# Inventory Item
# Example Business Knowledge expressed in Menata Language
# Domain: Warehouse — items stocked in multiple units of measure
# Case 5 of the Case Portfolio (runtime/case-portfolio.md)
# External benchmark: runtime/benchmarks/006-inventory-warehouse-benchmark.md
#
# Note: "Unit Conversions" below is a table-of-rows field. No Menata Language grammar
# for a child table/line-item field exists yet (CAP-F16 is a Runtime/Metadata gap
# today; this case surfaces it is a Language-layer gap too) — written provisionally
# as one Fields line, pending a formal grammar addition.
#
# Tier 1 of the Quantity/UoM framework (Study 15): Rice — Base Unit KG, one fixed
# alternate unit (SAK) — needs no row in Unit Conversions at all, see Stock Movement.
# Tier 2: Cement — Base Unit PCS, multiple alternate units (BOX, DOZEN) — needs the
# Unit Conversions table below.

Item

Fields

- Name : Text
- Base Unit : PCS | KG | BOX | SAK
- Minimum Stock Level : Number
- Stock On Hand : Number
- Unit Conversions : Table of (Unit, Factor)

Constraints

- Name is required.
- Base Unit is required.

Permissions

Warehouse Staff

- View

Views

- Item Form : Form
- Item List : List
- Low Stock Items : List
- Item Detail : Detail
